   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "6260fe59-04b2-440b-a8d4-7cb87d89d41f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import random"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "123a7b60-afbd-492f-9a2a-8c6d63f91105",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "What we want to achieve: to have a dataframe called stimuli.csv that we can import into lab.js. It will have a primes, a targets, and a conditions column.\n",
    "Why do we need this? Because it's much easier than typing it all in by hand into the lab.js interface\n",
    "\n",
    "How are we going to get this dataframe?\n",
    "    1. import the original dataframe\n",
    "    2. find stimuli pairs for each condition and create a new dataframe for each condition with the columns 'prime' and 'target' \n",
    "    3. create a new column that has the prime + target word pairs: this is 'combined'\n",
    "    4. create sets of unique word pairs for each condition from the 'combined' column\n",
    "    5. convert sets to lists and shuffle them\n",
    "    6. make each shuffled list the same length\n",
    "    7. re-split the pairs so they can be in their own columns - we need this for the stimuli.csv dataframe\n",
    "    8. putting the dataset together:\n",
    "        1. columns with all the primes, all the targets, and condition labels\n",
    "        2. create a datafram of these columns using pandas\n",
    "        3. save datafram to a csv to import it to lab.js\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5ab15d6a-8621-46ab-a2c9-0af0491a3905",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. import the original dataframe"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 25,
   "id": "b414b8bb-ef90-4f31-99d2-72110b969bd4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# we want to define where we want to get the original datafile from, \n",
    "# and where we're going to put the file that we created\n",
    "# we also want to give the names of the files\n",
    "\n",
    "pathin = \"/work/Lexical decision task/all ldt subs_all trials3.csv/\" # where we're getting the original data from\n",
    "pathout = \"/work/Lexical decision task/all ldt subs_all trials3.csv/\" # where we want to put the finished data\n",
    "\n",
    "infile = \"all ldt subs_all trials.csv\"\n",
    "outfile = \"stimuli.csv\" # name the file that will b e your finished dataframe: eg.: stimulus.csv"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
