   "source": [
    "2. find stimuli pairs for each condition and create a new dataframe for each condition with the columns 'prime' and 'target'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4c01f818-33bb-429a-8085-f8758a135940",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# create a new dataframe for the three conditions: related, unrelated, and nonword\n",
    "# step 1: what are the names of these columns in the dataframe?\n",
    "\n",
    "# df_condition1 = raw[(raw['C1'] == 'A') & raw(['C2'] == 'B')] [['X', 'Y']]\n",
    "# df_condition_nw = raw[raw['C1'] == 'C'] [['X', 'Y']]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6723c80c-db26-40a4-aeef-4a1851f60132",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "3. create a new column that has the prime + target word pairs: this is 'combined'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "52a8335f-8429-4181-acd4-126e16c088e1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# create a new column that combines the prime and target into a single string, \n",
    "# so we can easily identify unique pairs\n",
    "\n",
    "# df_condition1['combined'] = df_condition1['X'] + \" \" + df_condition1['Y']"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "030439a3-6170-474f-9aeb-384b93144925",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "4. create sets of unique word pairs for each condition from the 'combined' column"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "67299ab4-29bf-4385-93cb-a86836c11729",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# create sets of unique pairs for each condition\n",
    "# why do we need sets?\n",
    "# what type of collection variable are our pairs stored in now?\n",
    "# what do we have to do to make them into sets?\n",
    "\n",
    "# condition1 = "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4d72b9d5-d07f-49fc-9a94-04bd2d2e3e7d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
